<https://wealth.example.org/neowealth/declared-attribute/main/client_net_new_money/product_id> a meta:DeclaredAttribute ;
    meta:rawYaml """attribute_type: identifier
description: 'Declared join -> dim_product_unified_cat.product_id - which matches
  no row in this data (see below). This is the ONLY product-bearing fact table with
  NO isin - flows are tracked at product_id granularity only. In this data product_id
  holds 4 AGGREGATE codes, not catalogue product keys: AGG_BONDS (102 rows, product_type
  ''Bonds''), AGG_DIRECT_EQUITY (150, ''Direct Equity''), AGG_FIXED_DEPOSITS (180,
  ''Fixed Deposits''), AGG_MUTUAL_FUNDS (180, ''Mutual Funds''). NONE of the 612 rows
  matches a dim_product_unified_cat.product_id (individual products such as PROD_EQ_001),
  so the declared join returns no rows - and an equivalent query must keep returning
  none. Read the bucket from product_type on the same row. Whether AGG_* codes denote
  investment categories is not stated by the source and must be confirmed with the
  data team. A confirmed category relationship may be added separately; it must not
  replace this join or spread a category total across individual products. Preserve
  the original product_id, product_type, client and period values.'
display_name: Product ID
filterable: true
join_target: dim_product_unified_cat.product_id
name: product_id
nullable: true
sql_type: varchar(256)
type: string
""" .

